{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Lifecycle - System API - Okta API Token Revoked",
	"Description": "An Okta API token was revoked. Usually this is hygiene, but revoking the token a security tool authenticates with is a way to blind that tool, so check what the revoked token was used for.\n\nEvent type: system.api_token.revoke\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/impact_attempt_to_revoke_okta_api_token/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "14cab992-7602-5fa4-8ce8-5c0d7d80382f",
